        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2011",
        "question_text": "<p>Which heat treatment process is used to <b>increase the hardness</b> of steel?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Quenching is a heat treatment process where steel is rapidly cooled in water, oil, or air to increase its hardness. This process locks the carbon atoms in place, creating a hard but brittle structure.</p>",
